  The bundle plays asciicast v3 (the format the SSH channel records: i, o, r, m and x events) as well
  as v2, and runs its terminal emulator as WebAssembly, which is why the pages' Content-Security-Policy
  allows 'wasm-unsafe-eval' for scripts from Beacon itself and nothing else.

@openlinkos/ui, the design system the pages and the console are drawn with (its stylesheet, icons and
  the Geist fonts), is vendored under ol/, with its own NOTICE, licences and hashes; scripts/update-ui.sh
  refreshes it from npm.

beacon.css, beacon-brand.css and beacon-player.js are Beacon's own (Apache-2.0, see the repository's
LICENSE). beacon-brand.css is provisional: Beacon's accent until @openlinkos/ui ships data-brand="beacon".
